From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: ps5: A surface is its window's size again.

1045 answered every surface's capabilities with the scan-out's size
(1920x1080), because RADV's wsi_orbis could only register buffers of
that size and refused any other swapchain. That kept DXVK titles on
screen, but a GL title that draws at its window's size -- WON Half-Life
under Zink, a 640x480 window -- rendered into one corner of a 1920x1080
image while the display showed the whole image (2026-11-05, 01.11).

Mesa 0039 lets wsi_orbis take a swapchain of any size and fit it to the
screen (aspect kept, centred, black bars). So answer as upstream does: the
window's client rect, clamped to the scan-out. A window with no usable
size still gets the scan-out's. WINE_PS5_SURFACE_EXTENT=scanout restores
the forced extent for an A/B.

The SUBOPTIMAL-on-resize checks stay compiled out on PROSPERO.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1650,6 +1650,7 @@
     if (capabilities->currentExtent.width == 0xffffffff)
     {
         const char *scanout = getenv( "WINE_PS5_SCANOUT" );
+        const char *mode = getenv( "WINE_PS5_SURFACE_EXTENT" );
         unsigned int width, height;
 
         if (!scanout || sscanf( scanout, "%ux%u", &width, &height ) != 2 ||
@@ -1658,12 +1659,24 @@
             width = 1920;
             height = 1080;
         }
+        /* ⚠ THE WINDOW'S OWN SIZE, NOT THE SCREEN'S (2026-11-05, 1054). Forcing every surface to the
+         * scan-out made a GL title that draws at its window size (WON Half-Life, 640x480 under Zink)
+         * render into one corner of a 1920x1080 image. RADV's wsi_orbis now fits a swapchain of any
+         * size to the screen (Mesa 0039), so this answers as upstream does: the client rect, clamped
+         * to the scan-out. A window with no usable size still gets the scan-out.
+         * WINE_PS5_SURFACE_EXTENT=scanout restores the forced extent for an A/B. */
+        if (!(mode && !strcmp( mode, "scanout" )) &&
+            get_surface_rect( surface->hwnd, &client_rect, get_dpi_for_window( surface->hwnd ) ) &&
+            client_rect.right > 0 && client_rect.bottom > 0)
+        {
+            width = min( width, (unsigned int)client_rect.right );
+            height = min( height, (unsigned int)client_rect.bottom );
+        }
         capabilities->currentExtent.width = capabilities->minImageExtent.width =
             capabilities->maxImageExtent.width = width;
         capabilities->currentExtent.height = capabilities->minImageExtent.height =
             capabilities->maxImageExtent.height = height;
     }
-    (void)client_rect;
 #else
     /* Update the image extents to match what the Win32 WSI would provide. */
     /* FIXME: handle DPI scaling, somehow */
